    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "Option D (charcoal) is a processed solid fuel derived from biomass, which is often categorized with non-renewable or secondary fuels in basic science contexts, making it a less direct example than primary renewable sources.",
      "evidence": "Charcoal is produced via carbonization of wood; educational materials typically contrast direct renewable sources (wind/solar) with combustion of solid fuels.",
